      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    actual_values = [\n        150.2, 149.8, 150.5, 151.0, 150.7,\n        151.5, 152.0, 151.8, 152.3, 152.1\n    ]\n    expected_values = [\n        150.0, 150.1, 150.3, 150.9, 150.6,\n        151.3, 152.1, 151.9, 152.5, 152.0\n    ]\n\n    # Calculate residuals\n    residuals = [\n        actual - expected\n        for actual, expected in zip(actual_values, expected_values)\n    ]\n\n    # Calculate the Durbin-Watson statistic\n    squared_error_sum = sum(residual ** 2 for residual in residuals)\n    squared_difference_sum = sum(\n        (residuals[i] - residuals[i - 1]) ** 2\n        for i in range(1, len(residuals))\n    )\n    durbin_watson = squared_difference_sum / squared_error_sum\n\n    # Return the answer rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(durbin_watson, 2)\n```",
